===Alternative forms===
[[Image:Escaping criticism-by pere borrel del caso.png|thumb|Trompe l'oeil of a portrait subject escaping his frame.]]
* {{l|en|trompe l'œil|trompe l’œil}}, {{l|en|trompe-l'oeil|trompe-l’oeil}}, {{l|en|trompe-l'œil|trompe-l’œil}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|trompe-l’œil|lit=deceives the eye}}, from {{m|fr|trompe|t=deceives|pos=third-person singular present indicative of {{m|fr|tromper}}}} + {{m|fr|l’|t=the|pos=prevocalic form of {{m|fr|le}}}} + {{m|fr|œil||eye}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|tʀôɴp löy}}, {{IPA|en|/tʁɔ̃p lœj/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|[[trompe l'oeil|trompe l’oeil]]|trompe l’oeils|head=trompe l’oeil}} {{qualifier|see usage notes}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[genre]] of [[painting]] that exploits human [[vision]] to create the [[illusion]] that the [[subject]] of the painting is real.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A painting of this kind.
#* {{RQ:Bellow Humboldt's Gift|year=1976|page=74|passage=It looked like a private apartment, and yet it seemed also to be a place of business. It was furnished in decorative style with plastic, trick art objects hanging on the walls, geometrical forms of the '''''trompe l'oeil''''' type that intrigue business people. They are peculiarly vulnerable to art racketeers.}}

====Usage notes====
* This phrase is sometimes misconstructed as {{m|en|trompe d'œil|trompe d’œil}} and {{m|en|trompe-d'œil|trompe-d’œil}}, which, literally interpreted in French, means “deceives ''of'' eye”.
* In French, {{m|fr|trompe-l'œil|trompe-l’œil}} is an [[invariant]] noun; the same usage is reflected in the plural use of the English {{m|en||trompe l’oeil}}. Alternatively, {{m|en||trompe l’oeil}} is treated as a [[headless]] noun phrase, to which is suffixed {{m|en|-s}} to form a regular plural form. Still otherwise, some authors form novel plurals on modified etymological bases, such as the technically correct {{m|en|trompent-l'œil|trompent-l’œil|[they] deceive the eye}} and the ultimately mistaken {{m|en|trompe les yeux||deceives the eyes}}; however, such neologistic constructions are vanishingly rare.

